# Normalise line endings to LF in both the repository and the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. expo-updates' "fingerprint" runtimeVersion policy hashes
# file bytes, and eas.json is one of the inputs. With core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows, an ordinary `git checkout` rewrote eas.json with CRLF, which changed
# the Android fingerprint from f7eb033a to 79334b8d without changing a single
# character of content. Published OTA updates then carry a runtimeVersion that no
# installed build matches, so they are silently never delivered — no error on the
# phone, no error from `eas update`.
#
# EAS builds check out on Linux and therefore see LF, so LF is the canonical form
# and the working tree must match it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
